    "assessment": {
      "conclusion": "Retaining native FP32 math for this case is supported as a precision-plausible choice: its initial coefficients are three binary32 representable steps from the nearest FP32 direct-OLS coefficients, while the pinned-source coefficients are about 92\u2013103 local FP32 ULP from the same OLS. Re-evaluation shows 99.48% of the native/source R2 delta comes from fitted-parameter differences, not R2 evaluation; native R2 is much nearer independent FP64 OLS.",
      "environment_limit": "Focused replay used Python 3.12.3 standard-library binary32/binary64 decoding and math.fsum because NumPy/SciPy are unavailable in the current shell. The archived qualification used the recorded NumPy/SciPy versions and source hashes; pinned-source values were read from its diagnostic and their six source file hashes matched the receipt.",
